Package: toolfetch
Title: Browse and Install Tools from jackspepper/tools
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Jack", "Pepper", email = "jack.pepper@thekids.org.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Lists top-level tool folders in the jackspepper/tools GitHub
    repository, lets the user pick one interactively (or specify one
    directly for scripted use), and downloads it into the current working
    directory. Folders detected as R packages (via a top-level DESCRIPTION
    file) can be installed automatically via pak. Supports forced overwrite
    of existing downloads and fully non-interactive operation. Maintains a
    local cache of the repo's folder listing that refreshes weekly (or on
    demand) so repeated calls don't hit the GitHub API every time.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    httr2,
    utils
Suggests:
    pak,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
